This repository builds a static site. The site is the mjswan viewer plus scenes
and policies fetched at build time from the projects below, and a second page
(physics/) adapted from zalo/mujoco_wasm. Their license terms
are unchanged by being listed here. Per-scene LICENSE and NOTICE files written
into dist/ by the build sit beside the bytes they cover. The viewer also writes
dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for packages bundled into the browser engine, and
dist/LICENSE is mjswan's own Apache-2.0 license.

v1 does not ship assets whose terms are non-commercial, no-derivatives, or
unstated. microduck's STL meshes (recorded as CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) and the LAFAN1
dance clip (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) are not in the build. See the notes below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mjswan
https://github.com/ttktjmt/mjswan
License: Apache-2.0

Browser viewer (MuJoCo WASM, ONNX Runtime Web, three.js). Commercial use and
company pages are asked to keep the swan icon in the control panel and the
dialog it opens. This project does not remove them.

MuJoCo itself (the simulator compiled to WASM) is Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco

The engine build writes dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. From the build made
with mjswan 0.12.8, that file identifies:

- @ttktjmt/mujoco 3.11.0, Apache-2.0
- onnxruntime-web 1.29.0, MIT
- three 0.181.2, MIT
- jszip 3.10.1, SPDX "MIT OR GPL-3.0-or-later"

jszip is dual-licensed. This site uses it under MIT. Other bundled packages
are in the same file. Read it rather than this list if the mjswan version
changes.

